I’m implementing a balanced prime-coordinate quadratic form. A witness chooses exactly half the coordinates to receive the larger of two fixed nearby primes; the form vanishes exactly when the corresponding integer weights sum to zero. The planted half and its complement are generated independently from the same zero-sum distribution, so neither side has a marginal “plant” signature. This also gives a clean NP-hardness reduction from equal-cardinality partition and a compact rendered instance.
