Implemented and verified the problem generator based on the paper’s homogeneous prime-coordinate equations ([full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2310.02137v2)).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2310_02137.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2310.02137/gen_2310_02137.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2310.02137/selftest_report.json)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2310.02137/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2310.02137/README.md)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2310.02137/.meta.json)

Results:

- All G1–G8 gates pass.
- Structured random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Enumerable audit: exactly 2 solutions among 48,620 candidates.
- Three adversarial attacks: 0 successes across eight seeds.
- Canonical-key tests: 120/120 invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.
- Size-doubled instance at 120 variables builds and verifies.
- Hardening verdict: `hardened` at the 60-variable `easy` preset with no escalation.
- Gemini and Grok returned invalid witnesses; Claude exhausted its token limit without emitting an answer. This limitation is documented in the README.
